WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.346
This is your explainer on property relations between husband and wife: Articles

00:00:05.346 --> 00:00:10.093
seventy-four to one forty-eight of the Family Code, for Attorney Uribe's class.

00:00:10.623 --> 00:00:12.308
We'll go through Sir's five parts.

00:00:12.488 --> 00:00:16.158
One, marriage settlements and donations by reason of marriage.

00:00:16.338 --> 00:00:18.663
Two, the absolute community of property.

00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:21.168
Three, the conjugal partnership of gains.

00:00:21.348 --> 00:00:23.098
Four, separation of property.

00:00:23.278 --> 00:00:26.371
And five, property regimes of unions without marriage.

00:00:26.551 --> 00:00:30.028
I'll flag his quiz traps and his situationers along the way.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:36.367
Article seventy-four sets the order of governing rules: first, the marriage settlement

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:41.626
executed before the marriage; second, the Family Code; and third, local custom.

00:00:42.156 --> 00:00:46.270
If there's no settlement, or the regime agreed on is

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:50.383
void, Article seventy-five gives the default: absolute community of property

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:54.497
for marriages on or after August third, nineteen eighty-eight, and

00:00:54.497 --> 00:00:58.199
conjugal partnership of gains for marriages before that date.

00:00:58.729 --> 00:01:00.244
Sir loves this in quizzes.

00:01:00.424 --> 00:01:04.084
A statement that property relations are governed primarily by the

00:01:04.084 --> 00:01:07.378
Family Code is false, because the settlement comes first.

00:01:07.558 --> 00:01:11.569
And a statement that a couple with no settlement is under

00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:15.579
absolute community is false if the date of the marriage isn't

00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:19.590
given, because a pre-nineteen eighty-eight marriage defaults to the conjugal partnership.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.298
Remember his rule: if your answer is false, explain

00:01:22.298 --> 00:01:24.826
why it's false, not why it would be true.

00:01:25.906 --> 00:01:26.674
Form.

00:01:26.854 --> 00:01:31.184
Under Article seventy-seven, a marriage settlement must be in writing, signed

00:01:31.184 --> 00:01:35.515
by the parties, and executed before the celebration of the marriage.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:39.198
It binds third persons only if registered in the local

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:42.351
civil registry and in the proper registries of property.

00:01:42.881 --> 00:01:47.038
These are graded false every time: in a public instrument; executed

00:01:47.038 --> 00:01:50.817
during the celebration; or may be made before the celebration.

00:01:50.997 --> 00:01:53.642
Executing it before the wedding is mandatory.

00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:58.761
After the wedding, a settlement can be modified only through the court

00:01:58.761 --> 00:02:03.700
routes in Articles sixty-six, sixty-seven, one twenty-eight, one thirty-five and one thirty-six.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:08.860
Sir's minor situationer: a couple married in December nineteen eighty-nine, and the

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.105
bride was nineteen, with her parents not parties to the settlement.

00:02:13.285 --> 00:02:14.031
Valid?

00:02:14.211 --> 00:02:15.875
It depends on the exact date.

00:02:16.055 --> 00:02:19.582
Republic Act sixty-eight oh nine lowered the age

00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:22.669
of majority effective December eighteenth, nineteen eighty-nine.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:26.753
Before that, she was a minor, and Article seventy-eight required the persons

00:02:26.753 --> 00:02:30.657
who must consent to the marriage to be parties to the settlement.

00:02:31.187 --> 00:02:36.072
And under Article eighty, absent a contrary stipulation, Philippine law governs

00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:40.958
the property relations of Filipino spouses, wherever they married or live.

00:02:41.138 --> 00:02:43.550
A quiz statement that drops the words

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.618
absent a contrary stipulation is false.

00:02:46.697 --> 00:02:50.210
Donations by reason of marriage, under Article eighty-two, are

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:53.723
made before the celebration, in consideration of the marriage,

00:02:53.723 --> 00:02:57.236
and in favor of one or both future spouses.

00:02:57.416 --> 00:03:00.136
In Quiz four, a statement that said made by

00:03:00.136 --> 00:03:02.856
one or both of the future spouses was false.

00:03:03.036 --> 00:03:06.428
Anyone may be the donor; the future spouses are the donees.

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:08.750
As to form, nothing changed.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.875
Sir says the Family Code didn't alter the formalities, so the

00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:16.820
Civil Code rules apply: a movable worth over five thousand pesos

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:20.407
needs a writing, and an immovable needs a public document.

00:03:20.937 --> 00:03:24.923
If the marriage doesn't take place, Article eighty-one makes the

00:03:24.923 --> 00:03:28.510
stipulations in the settlement, including donations in it, void.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.933
Not revocable, and not revoked by operation of law.

00:03:32.113 --> 00:03:34.438
Sir: there's nothing to revoke if it's void.

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:38.020
Article eighty-four is his favorite one-fifth item.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.898
If the regime is other than absolute community, the future spouses

00:03:41.898 --> 00:03:45.595
can't donate to each other in their settlement more than one

00:03:45.595 --> 00:03:49.293
fifth of their present property, and only the excess is void.

00:03:49.473 --> 00:03:53.036
Donations of future property follow the rules on wills.

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:56.942
But Sir warns: just because there's no one-fifth cap

00:03:56.942 --> 00:03:59.944
under absolute community doesn't mean there's no limit.

00:04:00.124 --> 00:04:03.025
The rules on legitimes and donations still apply.

00:04:03.555 --> 00:04:07.875
And Article eighty-five: if donated property is encumbered and is foreclosed for

00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:12.195
less than the debt, the donee is not liable for the deficiency.

00:04:12.375 --> 00:04:15.042
If it sells for more, the donee gets the excess.

00:04:15.222 --> 00:04:17.014
The trap swaps donee for donor.

00:04:18.094 --> 00:04:22.365
Article eighty-six lists six grounds for the donor to revoke: the

00:04:22.365 --> 00:04:26.636
marriage isn't celebrated or is declared void, except donations in the

00:04:26.636 --> 00:04:30.907
settlement, which Article eighty-one already voids; the marriage took place without

00:04:30.907 --> 00:04:35.178
the parents' consent; the marriage is annulled and the donee acted

00:04:35.178 --> 00:04:39.448
in bad faith; legal separation, with the donee as the guilty

00:04:39.448 --> 00:04:43.331
spouse; a resolutory condition is fulfilled; and the donee's ingratitude.

00:04:43.511 --> 00:04:47.565
In Quiz four, each wrong option changed one word: advice

00:04:47.565 --> 00:04:51.213
for consent, donor for donee, or suspensive for resolutory.

00:04:51.743 --> 00:04:56.212
Article eighty-seven: donations between spouses during the marriage are void,

00:04:56.212 --> 00:05:00.234
except moderate gifts on the occasion of family rejoicing.

00:05:00.414 --> 00:05:04.723
The prohibition also covers couples living together without a valid marriage.

00:05:05.253 --> 00:05:08.943
That last sentence codifies Matabuena versus Cervantes, where

00:05:08.943 --> 00:05:12.634
a donation between common-law partners was struck down.

00:05:12.814 --> 00:05:16.182
And in Sir's Rolls-Royce situationer, a thirty-million-peso car

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:19.129
given to the wife: is that moderate?

00:05:19.309 --> 00:05:21.080
It depends on the family's means.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.945
Moderation is relative.

00:05:24.025 --> 00:05:26.137
Part two, the absolute community.

00:05:26.317 --> 00:05:29.983
It begins at the precise moment the marriage is celebrated;

00:05:29.983 --> 00:05:33.649
no waiver is allowed during the marriage except on judicial

00:05:33.649 --> 00:05:37.315
separation of property, and then only by a public instrument;

00:05:37.315 --> 00:05:40.248
and the suppletory rules are those on co-ownership.

00:05:40.777 --> 00:05:45.122
Under Article ninety-one, the community consists of all property owned

00:05:45.122 --> 00:05:49.033
at the celebration or acquired after, unless otherwise provided.

00:05:49.213 --> 00:05:53.157
Article ninety-two lists three exclusions: property acquired during the marriage

00:05:53.157 --> 00:05:57.102
by gratuitous title, with its fruits, unless the giver says

00:05:57.102 --> 00:06:01.046
otherwise; property for personal and exclusive use, except jewelry; and

00:06:01.046 --> 00:06:04.991
property owned before the marriage by a spouse who has

00:06:04.991 --> 00:06:08.541
legitimate descendants by a former marriage, with its fruits.

00:06:09.071 --> 00:06:13.658
His most repeated trap quotes Article ninety-one without the opening qualifier,

00:06:13.658 --> 00:06:18.244
unless otherwise provided in this Chapter or in the marriage settlements.

00:06:18.424 --> 00:06:20.174
Without it, the statement is false.

00:06:20.354 --> 00:06:24.364
And jewelry is never excluded, even if only one spouse uses it.

00:06:24.895 --> 00:06:29.780
The presumption in Article ninety-three applies to property acquired during the marriage.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.971
In Quiz four, the options were gratuitous, onerous, before the marriage, and

00:06:33.971 --> 00:06:37.982
registered during the marriage, and the answer was none of the above.

00:06:38.162 --> 00:06:40.316
Registration is not acquisition.

00:06:41.396 --> 00:06:44.361
Article ninety-four lists the community's charges.

00:06:44.541 --> 00:06:49.351
The highlights: support of the spouses, their common children, and the legitimate

00:06:49.351 --> 00:06:54.161
children of either spouse; debts for the community's benefit, and debts contracted

00:06:54.161 --> 00:06:58.971
without consent to the extent the family benefited; expenses to preserve separate

00:06:58.971 --> 00:07:03.781
property that is used by the family; antenuptial debts that redounded to

00:07:03.781 --> 00:07:08.591
the family's benefit; and, in paragraph nine, debts that didn't benefit the

00:07:08.591 --> 00:07:13.401
family, support of illegitimate children, and liabilities from crimes, which the community

00:07:13.401 --> 00:07:17.409
advances and then deducts from that spouse's share at liquidation.

00:07:17.589 --> 00:07:20.576
If the community is insufficient, the spouses

00:07:20.576 --> 00:07:23.563
are solidarily liable, except for paragraph nine.

00:07:24.093 --> 00:07:28.261
A midterm item said the community is liable for all expenses

00:07:28.261 --> 00:07:32.050
for mere preservation of the separate property of either spouse.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.470
False: it omits used by the family.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:37.237
And Sir corrected a student who said benefit of

00:07:37.237 --> 00:07:39.536
the family; the codal word here is used.

00:07:40.065 --> 00:07:43.339
Sir also asked: is there an expense chargeable to

00:07:43.339 --> 00:07:46.614
the absolute community but not to the conjugal partnership?

00:07:46.794 --> 00:07:49.269
Support of a spouse's illegitimate children.

00:07:49.449 --> 00:07:54.224
Under absolute community, almost everything becomes community property, so the spouse usually

00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:58.601
has nothing separate to pay from, and the community advances it.

00:07:59.131 --> 00:08:02.587
And Article ninety-five: gambling losses are borne by the

00:08:02.587 --> 00:08:06.043
losing spouse alone, while winnings go to the community.

00:08:07.123 --> 00:08:10.494
Administration is joint under Article ninety-six.

00:08:10.674 --> 00:08:14.663
If the spouses disagree, the husband's decision prevails, subject to the

00:08:14.663 --> 00:08:18.652
wife's recourse to the court within five years from the contract.

00:08:18.832 --> 00:08:22.459
A disposition or encumbrance without the other spouse's written consent

00:08:22.459 --> 00:08:26.085
or court authority is void, but it is treated as

00:08:26.085 --> 00:08:29.712
a continuing offer that the other spouse may still accept.

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:33.528
Either spouse may dispose of his or her interest by will.

00:08:33.708 --> 00:08:38.906
But neither may donate community property without the other's consent, except moderate

00:08:38.906 --> 00:08:43.671
donations for charity, or on occasions of family rejoicing or distress.

00:08:44.201 --> 00:08:49.332
Under Article ninety-nine, the community ends upon death, a decree of legal

00:08:49.332 --> 00:08:54.462
separation, annulment or a declaration of nullity, or judicial separation of property.

00:08:54.642 --> 00:08:56.936
But Sir stresses: if the marriage is

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:59.229
void, there never was an absolute community.

00:08:59.409 --> 00:09:02.491
Co-ownership under Article one forty-seven or one

00:09:02.491 --> 00:09:05.574
forty-eight governs, and there's nothing to dissolve.

00:09:06.104 --> 00:09:09.836
Mere separation in fact doesn't end the regime, but a spouse

00:09:09.836 --> 00:09:13.229
who leaves without just cause loses the right to support.

00:09:13.409 --> 00:09:17.298
And a spouse gone three months without informing the family is

00:09:17.298 --> 00:09:20.833
only prima facie presumed to have no intention of returning.

00:09:21.013 --> 00:09:23.232
A quiz statement that says deemed is false.

00:09:24.312 --> 00:09:28.748
On liquidation, Article one oh two sets six steps: inventory; pay

00:09:28.748 --> 00:09:33.183
the community's debts, with the spouses solidarily liable for any balance;

00:09:33.183 --> 00:09:37.619
return each spouse's exclusive property; divide the net remainder equally; deliver

00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:42.054
the common children's presumptive legitimes; and award the conjugal dwelling to

00:09:42.054 --> 00:09:46.490
the spouse the majority of the children choose, with children below

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:48.909
seven deemed to choose the mother.

00:09:49.089 --> 00:09:52.193
If a share is forfeited, the net profits are only

00:09:52.193 --> 00:09:55.297
the increase in market value from the wedding to dissolution.

00:09:55.827 --> 00:09:58.813
On death, Article one oh three requires liquidation

00:09:58.813 --> 00:10:01.800
in the estate proceeding, or within one year.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.714
Otherwise, later dispositions of the community property are void.

00:10:05.894 --> 00:10:10.417
And if the survivor remarries without liquidating, a mandatory regime of complete

00:10:10.417 --> 00:10:14.939
separation governs the new marriage, to protect the heirs of the deceased.

00:10:15.469 --> 00:10:16.578
Watch the period.

00:10:16.758 --> 00:10:18.764
Absolute community: one year.

00:10:18.944 --> 00:10:22.698
Conjugal partnership: six months, under Article one thirty.

00:10:22.878 --> 00:10:26.654
Tolentino's book prints one year for both; answer with the codal.

00:10:27.185 --> 00:10:30.689
And Article one oh four, applied in Delizo versus Delizo:

00:10:30.689 --> 00:10:34.193
when two marriages of the same person are liquidated together

00:10:34.193 --> 00:10:37.697
and you can't tell which community owns a property, divide

00:10:37.697 --> 00:10:41.201
it in proportion to the capital and duration of each.

00:10:42.281 --> 00:10:44.841
Part three, the conjugal partnership of gains.

00:10:45.021 --> 00:10:49.970
It applies by settlement, or by default to marriages before August third,

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:54.920
nineteen eighty-eight, and its suppletory rules are those on partnership, not co-ownership.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:58.780
The core idea: each spouse keeps what he or she

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:02.460
brings or receives gratuitously, and the partnership gets the gains.

00:11:02.989 --> 00:11:07.179
Article one oh nine lists the exclusive property: what each brings

00:11:07.179 --> 00:11:11.368
to the marriage; what each acquires during the marriage by gratuitous

00:11:11.368 --> 00:11:15.558
title; what is acquired by redemption, barter or exchange with exclusive

00:11:15.558 --> 00:11:18.605
property; and what is bought with exclusive money.

00:11:18.785 --> 00:11:23.581
Article one seventeen lists the conjugal property: onerous acquisitions from the

00:11:23.581 --> 00:11:28.378
common fund; earnings from labor or profession; fruits of common property

00:11:28.378 --> 00:11:33.174
and the net fruits of each spouse's exclusive property; and shares

00:11:33.174 --> 00:11:36.662
in hidden treasure, occupation, excess livestock and winnings.

00:11:37.193 --> 00:11:39.031
That third item is the trap Sir

00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:40.606
has asked at least five times.

00:11:40.786 --> 00:11:45.008
In a conjugal partnership, rentals from a spouse's exclusive property

00:11:45.008 --> 00:11:48.808
are conjugal, regardless of how that property was acquired.

00:11:49.887 --> 00:11:53.498
Article one sixteen: all property acquired during the marriage

00:11:53.498 --> 00:11:57.109
is presumed conjugal unless the contrary is proved, even

00:11:57.109 --> 00:12:00.319
if it's registered in only one spouse's name.

00:12:00.849 --> 00:12:02.812
But the presumption needs a foundation.

00:12:02.992 --> 00:12:06.242
In Torela, Dela Peña versus Avila, and Andrade versus

00:12:06.242 --> 00:12:09.491
Tan, the Court held that whoever invokes it must

00:12:09.491 --> 00:12:12.741
first prove the property was acquired during the marriage.

00:12:12.921 --> 00:12:14.679
Once that's shown, you don't need to

00:12:14.679 --> 00:12:16.185
prove the source of the funds.

00:12:16.715 --> 00:12:20.094
And in Magallon versus Montejo, a title saying

00:12:20.094 --> 00:12:23.051
married to so-and-so merely describes civil status.

00:12:23.231 --> 00:12:25.428
It doesn't prove the property is conjugal.

00:12:25.959 --> 00:12:28.572
Sir's situationer: you're counsel for the widow, and

00:12:28.572 --> 00:12:31.186
the title is in the late husband's name.

00:12:31.366 --> 00:12:33.296
Your best argument is that the land

00:12:33.296 --> 00:12:35.227
is hers alone, bought with her money.

00:12:35.407 --> 00:12:37.988
Your next best argument is that it's conjugal.

00:12:38.168 --> 00:12:42.075
And always answer the question asked: if he asks the nature of

00:12:42.075 --> 00:12:45.656
the property, say exclusive or conjugal, not just who gets it.

00:12:46.736 --> 00:12:50.825
Property bought on installments, under Article one eighteen, belongs to the

00:12:50.825 --> 00:12:54.914
buyer if full ownership vested before the marriage, and to the

00:12:54.914 --> 00:12:59.003
partnership if it vested during the marriage, with reimbursement either way.

00:12:59.183 --> 00:13:01.572
A midterm pair statement saying it always

00:13:01.572 --> 00:13:03.620
belongs to the partnership was false.

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:08.036
For credits payable in installments, under Article one nineteen, collections

00:13:08.036 --> 00:13:11.921
on the principal belong to the creditor-spouse, while interest falling

00:13:11.921 --> 00:13:15.030
due during the marriage goes to the partnership.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.099
Article one twenty is reverse accession.

00:13:18.279 --> 00:13:22.019
When the partnership improves one spouse's separate property, compare the cost

00:13:22.019 --> 00:13:25.759
of the improvement plus the resulting increase in value with the

00:13:25.759 --> 00:13:29.159
value of the property at the time of the improvement.

00:13:29.339 --> 00:13:32.688
If the improvement side is bigger, the whole

00:13:32.688 --> 00:13:36.037
property becomes conjugal, subject to reimbursing the owner-spouse.

00:13:36.217 --> 00:13:39.652
Otherwise, the owner-spouse keeps it and reimburses the cost.

00:13:39.832 --> 00:13:44.013
Either way, ownership vests only upon reimbursement at liquidation.

00:13:44.543 --> 00:13:48.365
For example: a lot worth five million; the partnership builds a

00:13:48.365 --> 00:13:51.839
house costing three million that adds one million in value.

00:13:52.019 --> 00:13:55.163
Four million is less than five, so the spouse keeps

00:13:55.163 --> 00:13:57.992
the lot and house and reimburses the three million.

00:13:59.073 --> 00:14:02.857
The charges on the partnership in Articles one twenty-one

00:14:02.857 --> 00:14:06.220
and one twenty-two mirror Article ninety-four, with differences.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.741
The preservation of separate property has no used by the family

00:14:10.741 --> 00:14:15.082
condition, and the solidary liability clause has no exception for advances.

00:14:15.262 --> 00:14:19.998
Personal debts are chargeable only if they benefited the family, while fines

00:14:19.998 --> 00:14:24.734
and support of illegitimate children are paid subsidiarily and charged at liquidation.

00:14:25.264 --> 00:14:29.264
On benefit to the family: in Luzon Surety versus de Garcia,

00:14:29.264 --> 00:14:32.901
the benefit must be clear and not fanciful or remote.

00:14:33.081 --> 00:14:37.238
In Carlos versus Abelardo, a loan used to buy the family

00:14:37.238 --> 00:14:41.017
home benefited the family, so the husband was solidarily liable.

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:45.836
Administration under Article one twenty-four is the same as Article

00:14:45.836 --> 00:14:50.125
ninety-six: joint, the husband's decision prevails subject to the wife's

00:14:50.125 --> 00:14:54.415
five-year recourse, and a disposition without written consent or court

00:14:54.415 --> 00:14:57.846
authority is void, though it's a continuing offer.

00:14:58.376 --> 00:14:59.571
Know the transition.

00:14:59.751 --> 00:15:03.857
Under the Civil Code, a sale of conjugal property without

00:15:03.857 --> 00:15:07.964
consent was only voidable, within ten years, as in Felipe

00:15:07.964 --> 00:15:11.249
versus Heirs of Aldon and Aguilar-Reyes versus Mijares.

00:15:11.429 --> 00:15:14.597
The date of the sale decides which rule applies:

00:15:14.597 --> 00:15:17.765
a sale after August third, nineteen eighty-eight is void.

00:15:18.845 --> 00:15:22.888
The conjugal partnership ends on the same events as the absolute

00:15:22.888 --> 00:15:26.930
community, and separation in fact and abandonment work the same way.

00:15:27.461 --> 00:15:32.510
Liquidation under Article one twenty-nine has nine steps: inventory; credit the partnership

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:37.560
for advances it made on personal debts; reimburse each spouse for exclusive

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:42.609
funds used; pay the conjugal debts; return the exclusive property; indemnify lost

00:15:42.609 --> 00:15:47.658
or deteriorated movables that were used for the family; divide the net

00:15:47.658 --> 00:15:51.866
profits equally; deliver presumptive legitimes; and award the conjugal dwelling.

00:15:52.396 --> 00:15:55.728
On death, Article one thirty: liquidate in the estate

00:15:55.728 --> 00:15:58.689
proceeding or within six months, not one year.

00:15:58.869 --> 00:16:02.379
Otherwise later dispositions are void, and remarriage

00:16:02.379 --> 00:16:05.888
without liquidation triggers mandatory separation of property.

00:16:06.418 --> 00:16:10.703
And under Article one thirty-three, as applied in Santero, the survivor

00:16:10.703 --> 00:16:14.987
and the children receive support from the common mass during liquidation,

00:16:14.987 --> 00:16:18.493
without distinction, even if the children are of age.

00:16:19.573 --> 00:16:21.578
Part four, separation of property.

00:16:21.758 --> 00:16:26.163
Article one thirty-four: unless the settlement expressly provides otherwise,

00:16:26.163 --> 00:16:30.569
separation during the marriage happens only by judicial order.

00:16:30.749 --> 00:16:33.266
It may be voluntary or for sufficient cause.

00:16:33.796 --> 00:16:38.823
Article one thirty-five lists six causes: civil interdiction, judicial declaration of absence,

00:16:38.823 --> 00:16:43.851
or loss of parental authority of the other spouse, where the final

00:16:43.851 --> 00:16:48.878
judgment is enough; abandonment or failure to comply with marital obligations; abuse

00:16:48.878 --> 00:16:53.906
of the power of administration granted in the settlement; and separation in

00:16:53.906 --> 00:16:58.095
fact for at least one year, with reconciliation highly improbable.

00:16:58.275 --> 00:17:00.618
Watch the number: one year here, but

00:17:00.618 --> 00:17:02.627
three months for the abandonment presumption.

00:17:03.157 --> 00:17:08.853
A voluntary separation under Article one thirty-six is by joint verified petition.

00:17:09.033 --> 00:17:11.638
No cause is needed, but all creditors must

00:17:11.638 --> 00:17:13.918
be listed in the petition and notified.

00:17:14.448 --> 00:17:18.806
In the twenty oh five bar, Gabby and Mila signed a

00:17:18.806 --> 00:17:22.768
private document dissolving their conjugal partnership and adopting complete separation.

00:17:22.948 --> 00:17:25.167
It was void; the partnership continued.

00:17:25.347 --> 00:17:28.035
Separation during the marriage needs a court order.

00:17:29.115 --> 00:17:33.567
When the court decrees separation, the regime is liquidated; support pending

00:17:33.567 --> 00:17:38.018
the case comes from the common property; complete separation governs after

00:17:38.018 --> 00:17:42.470
that; the decree is recorded; and creditors' prior rights are preserved.

00:17:42.999 --> 00:17:46.211
The former regime may be revived under Article one

00:17:46.211 --> 00:17:49.424
forty-one, by motion in the same proceeding, on any

00:17:49.424 --> 00:17:52.279
of seven grounds, with an agreement under oath.

00:17:52.459 --> 00:17:55.285
And after a voluntary separation has been

00:17:55.285 --> 00:17:58.112
revived, no further voluntary separation is allowed.

00:17:58.643 --> 00:18:00.713
Sir asked whether a settlement is the

00:18:00.713 --> 00:18:02.782
only way to get separation of property.

00:18:02.962 --> 00:18:03.644
No.

00:18:03.824 --> 00:18:07.963
Separation also arises by law when a survivor remarries

00:18:07.963 --> 00:18:12.102
without liquidating, after legal separation, and by judicial decree.

00:18:12.631 --> 00:18:17.713
Under the regime of separation, Articles one forty-three to one forty-six: it

00:18:17.713 --> 00:18:22.796
may cover present or future property, wholly or partly, and whatever isn't

00:18:22.796 --> 00:18:27.031
separated falls under the absolute community, not the conjugal partnership.

00:18:27.211 --> 00:18:30.089
Each spouse manages and disposes of his or

00:18:30.089 --> 00:18:32.608
her own property without the other's consent.

00:18:32.788 --> 00:18:36.223
Family expenses are shared in proportion to income, and

00:18:36.223 --> 00:18:39.658
the spouses are solidarily liable to creditors for them.

00:18:40.188 --> 00:18:44.206
And remember the form ladder Sir likes to test: a settlement needs

00:18:44.206 --> 00:18:48.223
only a writing; a waiver of one's share needs a public instrument;

00:18:48.223 --> 00:18:52.241
and a revival agreement must be under oath and filed in court.

00:18:53.321 --> 00:18:55.369
Part five, unions without marriage.

00:18:55.549 --> 00:18:57.341
Start with the threshold question.

00:18:57.521 --> 00:18:58.908
Is there a valid marriage?

00:18:59.088 --> 00:19:02.950
If the marriage is valid, or voidable and not yet

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:06.812
annulled, the spouses have an absolute community or conjugal partnership,

00:19:06.812 --> 00:19:10.288
and Articles one forty-seven and one forty-eight don't apply.

00:19:10.818 --> 00:19:12.994
If there's no valid marriage, ask whether

00:19:12.994 --> 00:19:15.170
either party is married to someone else.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:17.462
If so, it's Article one forty-eight.

00:19:17.992 --> 00:19:21.540
Otherwise, ask whether they're capacitated to marry each other and

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:24.733
living exclusively with each other as husband and wife.

00:19:24.913 --> 00:19:29.521
If yes, it's Article one forty-seven; if not, Article one forty-eight.

00:19:30.051 --> 00:19:34.281
Sir's rule of thumb: if one or both are married to other

00:19:34.281 --> 00:19:38.158
persons, a third person is affected, and Article one forty-eight applies.

00:19:38.338 --> 00:19:41.399
For every other ground of nullity where no

00:19:41.399 --> 00:19:44.460
third person is affected, apply Article one forty-seven.

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:48.459
So first cousins who married fall under one forty-seven, in his view.

00:19:48.989 --> 00:19:53.803
But many commentators, including Tolentino, put any impediment between the parties

00:19:53.803 --> 00:19:58.618
themselves, like first cousins or a party under eighteen, under Article

00:19:58.618 --> 00:20:03.432
one forty-eight, since one forty-seven requires capacity to marry each other.

00:20:03.612 --> 00:20:06.534
In Sir's class, apply his test and explain why.

00:20:07.615 --> 00:20:09.258
Now compare the two articles.

00:20:09.438 --> 00:20:13.675
Under Article one forty-seven, wages and salaries are owned in

00:20:13.675 --> 00:20:17.912
equal shares, and property acquired during the cohabitation is co-owned

00:20:17.912 --> 00:20:21.726
and presumed acquired by joint efforts, in equal shares.

00:20:21.906 --> 00:20:25.777
Under Article one forty-eight, wages belong to the earner,

00:20:25.777 --> 00:20:29.647
and there's co-ownership only of property acquired by actual

00:20:29.647 --> 00:20:32.658
joint contribution, in proportion to the contributions.

00:20:33.187 --> 00:20:37.461
Under one forty-seven, a party who cared for the family and household

00:20:37.461 --> 00:20:41.379
is deemed to have contributed; under one forty-eight, that doesn't count.

00:20:41.559 --> 00:20:45.623
And a bad-faith party's share is forfeited: under one forty-seven, to

00:20:45.623 --> 00:20:49.687
the common children, then descendants, then the innocent party; under one

00:20:49.687 --> 00:20:53.751
forty-eight, to the community or partnership of the valid marriage, and

00:20:53.751 --> 00:20:57.815
the forfeiture applies even if both parties are in bad faith.

00:20:58.345 --> 00:21:03.331
Article one forty-seven cases: in Maxey, decided under the old Article one

00:21:03.331 --> 00:21:07.902
forty-four, the partners shared equally even though only the man worked.

00:21:08.082 --> 00:21:12.178
Salas versus Aguila applied the presumption of joint acquisition.

00:21:12.358 --> 00:21:15.046
And Valdes holds that an Article thirty-six

00:21:15.046 --> 00:21:17.734
void marriage is liquidated as a co-ownership.

00:21:18.265 --> 00:21:22.603
Article one forty-eight cases: in Juaniza versus Jose, the man was married

00:21:22.603 --> 00:21:26.940
to someone else, so his partner could not be a co-owner of

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:31.278
the jeepney; it belonged to his conjugal partnership with his legal wife.

00:21:31.458 --> 00:21:35.917
In Cariño, the bigamous second wife got nothing without proof of contribution.

00:21:36.097 --> 00:21:39.894
And in Go-Bangayan, married to in a title was merely descriptive.

00:21:40.424 --> 00:21:42.365
Sir's situationer pulls it together.

00:21:42.545 --> 00:21:44.167
A marriage is declared void.

00:21:44.347 --> 00:21:48.400
During the cohabitation, A saved a million pesos from his wages,

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:52.453
a condo was bought with his income, and B inherited land.

00:21:52.633 --> 00:21:53.700
Who owns what?

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:55.992
It depends on why the marriage was void.

00:21:56.172 --> 00:22:00.293
Under one forty-seven, the savings and condo are shared equally;

00:22:00.293 --> 00:22:04.001
under one forty-eight, they're A's unless B proves contribution.

00:22:04.181 --> 00:22:06.955
Either way, the inherited land is B's alone.

00:22:08.035 --> 00:22:08.974
Let's recap.

00:22:09.154 --> 00:22:12.794
One: the order is settlement, Family Code, then custom,

00:22:12.794 --> 00:22:16.435
and the default is absolute community only for marriages

00:22:16.435 --> 00:22:19.266
on or after August third, nineteen eighty-eight.

00:22:19.446 --> 00:22:22.721
Two: a settlement must be in writing, signed, and

00:22:22.721 --> 00:22:25.632
executed before the wedding; not a public instrument.

00:22:25.812 --> 00:22:30.063
Three: donations are in favor of the future spouses; the

00:22:30.063 --> 00:22:34.315
one-fifth cap applies only to regimes other than absolute community;

00:22:34.315 --> 00:22:37.716
and Article eighty-one makes them void, not revocable.

00:22:38.246 --> 00:22:42.982
Four: Article ninety-one needs its qualifier, and jewelry is never excluded.

00:22:43.162 --> 00:22:48.154
Five: the presumption is triggered by acquisition during the marriage, not registration.

00:22:48.334 --> 00:22:52.275
Six: under absolute community, preservation of separate property is chargeable

00:22:52.275 --> 00:22:55.822
only if the property is used by the family.

00:22:56.352 --> 00:23:01.294
Seven: in the conjugal partnership, rentals of exclusive property are conjugal, and

00:23:01.294 --> 00:23:05.824
Article one twenty compares cost plus increase with the property's value.

00:23:06.004 --> 00:23:09.505
Eight: after death, liquidate within one year for absolute

00:23:09.505 --> 00:23:12.617
community and six months for the conjugal partnership.

00:23:13.147 --> 00:23:16.835
Nine: separation during the marriage needs a court order, and separation

00:23:16.835 --> 00:23:20.187
in fact as a cause requires at least one year.

00:23:20.367 --> 00:23:24.230
And ten: for unions without marriage, ask whether a third

00:23:24.230 --> 00:23:28.093
person is affected; wages are shared equally under one forty-seven

00:23:28.093 --> 00:23:31.183
but belong to the earner under one forty-eight.

00:23:31.363 --> 00:23:32.771
Good luck in recitation.
